  "solution": {
    "text": "When sulphuryl chloride $\\left(\\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\right)$, reacts with white phosphorus $\\left(\\mathrm{P}_{4}\\right),$ it give phosphorus pentachloride $\\left(\\mathrm{PCl}_{5}\\right)$ and sulphur dioxide $\\left(\\mathrm{SO}_{2}\\right)$. The reaction is as follows:\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{P}_{4}+10 \\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\longrightarrow 4 \\mathrm{PCl}_{5}+10 \\mathrm{SO}_{2}\r\n$$",
